      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "Siddhartha Gautama, who was both a prince and an ascetic, had to renounce
    both extremes to follow the middle path, ultimately attaining enlightenment under
    the Bodhi tree. \nOut of compassion, he decided to share what he had learned,
    and many have benefited from his teachings. \nShariputra and Maudgaly\u0101yana
    were two of his principal disciples, who were childhood friends, and both attained
    enlightenment through the Buddha's guidance. \n\u0100nanda and Mah\u0101k\u0101syapa
    were also important disciples; they attained enlightenment and helped others
    end suffering and achieve liberation.\nTheir path to enlightenment has been a
    source of inspiration for countless people throughout history.\r"
  m_isRightToLeft: 0
