  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 6fcfa33f6716de74186df78a67de7d5d, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  textMesh: {fileID: 1685533464}
  lessons:
  - _ There are people who have attained enlightenment.
  - _  Life involves suffering. Nothing is completely and permanently satisfying.
  - _ Wanting what we don't have and clinging to what we have is the root of unhappiness.
  - _ It is possible to stop suffering; in fact, it has already been achieved.
  - _ To free oneself from suffering, one must avoid extremes and live in balance.
  - _ Burning herbs facilitates concentration and meditation.
  - _Meditation clears away inner darkness, revealing the path.
  - _ One must learn to listen in order to learn from the environment.
  - _ Buddha taught others out of compassion how to untie themselves from suffering.
  - _ Each person is part of a whole, like currents within a single river.
  speed: 50
  journalCanvas: {fileID: 701195945}
  pauseMenu: {fileID: 982604114}
  writingLesson_Audio: {fileID: 1481314275}
  showingLesson_Audio: {fileID: 1184010233}
